    /// plain HTTP. If you return a mutated <c>Request</c>, make sure it still
    /// carries the original <c>Upgrade: websocket</c> and <c>Sec-WebSocket-*</c>
    /// headers — the simplest safe recipe is to clone the incoming
    /// request's headers (via <c>new Headers(req.headers)</c>) and only add
    /// or replace entries, rather than constructing a fresh <c>Headers</c>
    /// object from scratch.
